 \label{sec:analysis_triggers}
 
 The ATLAS Run~2 trigger architecture was described in Chapter~\ref{chapter:LHC_ATLAS_experiment}.
-Only the trigger selections used specifically in this analysis are discussed here. In general, the selection of triggers for each region is decided considering signal efficiency and the background rejection.
+This analysis uses only single-electron, single-muon and $\met$ triggers.
+The trigger selection for each region balances efficiency for the targeted final state against background rejection.
 
 The signal-region event selection uses the lowest-threshold unprescaled $\met$ trigger, which is fully efficient for offline $\met>200~\GeV$.
-Meanwhile, the offline $\met$ thresholds in all signal regions are applied at least $200~\GeV$, then ensuring full signal efficiency.
+Since all signal regions require offline $\met$ above at least $200~\GeV$, their selections lie within this trigger-efficiency plateau.
 The same $\met$ trigger strategy is used for the corresponding validation regions.
 
-The lowest-threshold unprescaled single-electron and single-muon triggers~\cite{ATLASElectronTriggerRun2,ATLASMuonTriggerRun2} are used in the  regions containing an electron or muon, while the lepton trigger threshold is approximately $26~\GeV$,.
+Single-electron and single-muon triggers are used in regions containing an electron or muon.
+The low-threshold single-lepton chains require electron $E_{\mathrm{T}}>24~\GeV$ or muon $\pT>20~\GeV$ in 2015; the thresholds increase to $26~\GeV$ during 2016 and remain at this value in 2017--2018~\cite{ATLASElectronTriggerRun2,ATLASMuonTriggerRun2}.
+The corresponding $\met$ trigger thresholds range from $70~\GeV$ in 2015 to $110~\GeV$ in the later Run~2 periods~\cite{ATLASMETTriggerRun2}.
+Table~\ref{tab:run2_trigger_chains} lists the relevant low-threshold chains in the Run~2 reference menu.
+
+In an HLT chain name, \texttt{e}, \texttt{mu} and \texttt{xe} identify an electron, a muon and $\met$, respectively; the following number gives the online threshold in GeV.
+An explicit \texttt{L1} suffix identifies the first-level trigger that seeds the chain.
+The electron labels \texttt{lhmedium} and \texttt{lhtight} specify likelihood-based identification requirements, while \texttt{nod0} indicates that transverse-impact-parameter information is omitted.
+The labels \texttt{iloose}, \texttt{ivarloose} and \texttt{ivarmedium} specify isolation requirements, with \texttt{var} denoting a cone size that decreases with lepton $\pT$.
+For $\met$, \texttt{mht} denotes a calculation based on the negative vector sum of jet transverse momenta, whereas \texttt{pufit} denotes a calorimeter-based calculation with a fit-based pile-up correction~\cite{ATLASElectronTriggerRun2,ATLASMuonTriggerRun2,ATLASMETTriggerRun2}.
 
